<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n88529" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσᾰναγκ-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>force</i> or <i>constrain besides</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.18
			</span></i>; <i>compress too tightly</i>, of a bandage, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Off.</u>
				8
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			); <i>force</i> bones <i>together</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαναγκάζω</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Art.</u>
				14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>increase the severity</i> of exercises, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ κούφων π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Vict.</u>
				3.68
			</span></i>; of military training, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ ἄλλῃ μελέτῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.72
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> c. acc. et
				inf., <i>force</i> one <i>to do</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίῃ με προσηνάγκασσε πάσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Cer.</u>
					413
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τινὰ παρεῖναι, μένειν,
				ὁμολογεῖν, φιλεῖν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.1.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				217d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				223d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Prt.</u>
				346b
			</span></i>: the inf. is freq. omitted, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς μὴ δεχομένους τὰς σπονδὰς π</span>.
			(sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέχεσθαι</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.42
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τινά τι</span>
			<i>force</i> him <i>also</i> (to do) something, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				181e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>constrain</i> or <i>compel</i> by argument, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ λόγῳ τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phlb.</u>
					13b
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				9.936
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τι εἶναι</span>
			<i>prove that</i> a thing <i>necessarily</i> is, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				710a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Plt.</u>
				284b
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
